tropy changes in healthy volunteers during remifentanil infusion</article-title><source>Anesthesiology</source><year>2006</year><volume>104</volume><fpage>921</fpage><lpage>932</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16645442</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00000542-200605000-00006</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Muncaster</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name><name><surname>Sleigh</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Changes in consciousness, conceptual memory, and quantitative electroencephalographical measures during recovery from sevoflurane- and remifentanil-based anesthesia</article-title><source>Anesth Analg</source><year>2003</year><volume>96</volume><fpage>720</fpage><lpage>725</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12598252</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1213/01.ANE.0000040143.95962.36</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>